        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): guard readFields JSON.parse against malformed CLI input",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`extensions/browser/src/cli/browser-cli-actions-input/shared.ts:97` calls bare `JSON.parse(payload)` in `readFields()` when parsing `--fields` or `--fields-file` CLI input. Malformed user input → raw `SyntaxError` instead of descriptive validation error.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `shared.ts`: wrap `JSON.parse(payload)` in try/catch, throw `Error(\"fields must be valid JSON.\")` instead of raw SyntaxError\n- `test/_proof_browser_cli_shared_json_guard.mts`: standalone proof script (8/8 PASS)\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal | AI-assisted\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ node --import tsx test/_proof_browser_cli_shared_json_guard.mts\n\n[1] malformed JSON fields → descriptive Error\n  PASS  throws Error (not SyntaxError)\n  PASS  message includes \"must be valid JSON\"\n\n[2] valid JSON fields array → returns correctly\n  PASS  no error thrown\n  PASS  returns array\n  PASS  returns 1 field\n\n[3] empty fields string → throws validation Error\n  PASS  throws Error for empty fields\n\n[4] valid JSON non-array → throws validation Error\n  PASS  throws Error for non-array\n  PASS  message is schema error (not JSON parse error)\n\n==================================================\n  Passed: 8  Failed: 0  Total: 8\n==================================================\n```\n\nBefore: `readFields({ fields: \"NOT JSON\" })` → raw SyntaxError\nAfter: `readFields({ fields: \"NOT JSON\" })` → `Error: fields must be valid JSON.`",
        "branch": "fix/browser-cli-shared-json-parse-guard",
